From: Protector of Earth Recomp
Subject: [PATCH] Pad backend: WASD drives the left analog stick

What broke:
  In Ben 10: Protector of Earth's first level the player character did not
  move from the keyboard. The pad backend (PSPadBackend::readState) always
  reports DualShock (analog) mode, but mapped W/A/S/D to the D-pad, the
  same as the arrow keys, and left both sticks centred. A gdb read of the
  data the game gets from scePadRead showed mode 0x73, the D-pad bit set
  for both W and Up, and the sticks at 0x80: the game moves the player only
  with the left stick.

Why:
  The keyboard map in Kernel/Stubs/Pad.cpp already documents "Analog left:
  WASD", but that path is only used when the backend has no data; the
  backend has its own map, where WASD doubled the arrows.

The fix:
  Arrows stay the D-pad; W/A/S/D set the left stick (data[6] = X, data[7]
  = Y) to full tilt (0x00 or 0xFF, 0x80 when neither or both keys of an
  axis are held), the same convention as the stub's map.
  Tested in the game: holding W makes the player walk forward (findings/18
  s.13). No automated test: the backend reads the keys through the host
  window library, which the test executable does not drive.

--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_pad.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_pad.cpp
@@ -89,14 +89,23 @@
     }
     else
     {
-        if (IsKeyDown(KEY_UP) || IsKeyDown(KEY_W))
+        // Arrows: the D-pad. WASD: the left analog stick (full tilt), as the keyboard map in
+        // Kernel/Stubs/Pad.cpp documents. This backend always reports analog (DualShock) mode,
+        // and games that move the player only with the left stick (Ben 10: Protector of Earth)
+        // could not be played from the keyboard while WASD only doubled the D-pad.
+        if (IsKeyDown(KEY_UP))
             clearBit(PAD_UP);
-        if (IsKeyDown(KEY_DOWN) || IsKeyDown(KEY_S))
+        if (IsKeyDown(KEY_DOWN))
             clearBit(PAD_DOWN);
-        if (IsKeyDown(KEY_LEFT) || IsKeyDown(KEY_A))
+        if (IsKeyDown(KEY_LEFT))
             clearBit(PAD_LEFT);
-        if (IsKeyDown(KEY_RIGHT) || IsKeyDown(KEY_D))
+        if (IsKeyDown(KEY_RIGHT))
             clearBit(PAD_RIGHT);
+        // data[6] = left stick X (0x00 left .. 0xFF right), data[7] = left stick Y (0x00 up).
+        const int stickX = (IsKeyDown(KEY_D) ? 1 : 0) - (IsKeyDown(KEY_A) ? 1 : 0);
+        const int stickY = (IsKeyDown(KEY_S) ? 1 : 0) - (IsKeyDown(KEY_W) ? 1 : 0);
+        data[6] = stickX < 0 ? 0x00 : (stickX > 0 ? 0xFF : kPadStickCenter);
+        data[7] = stickY < 0 ? 0x00 : (stickY > 0 ? 0xFF : kPadStickCenter);
         if (IsKeyDown(KEY_X) || IsKeyDown(KEY_SPACE))
             clearBit(PAD_CROSS);
         if (IsKeyDown(KEY_C) || IsKeyDown(KEY_ESCAPE))
